# Patterns to strip from the staging tree before publishing to the public
# GitHub mirror at aws-solutions-library-samples/guidance-for-connected-mobility-on-aws.
#
# Format: gitignore-syntax. Comments start with `#`. Trailing slash = directory.
# scripts/publish-to-github.sh applies these via find -path during the
# `strip` step (see scripts/publish-to-github.sh).

# Internal-only directories
.kiro/
issues/
.publish-history/

# Defense-in-depth: explicit exclusion of OEM1 spec decisions.md (which
# contains the internal-only OEM1 → vendor mapping). The .kiro/ directory
# exclusion above already covers this; the explicit entry survives if the
# directory-level exclusion is ever loosened.
.kiro/specs/2026-06-01-cms-oem1-transform-manifest-staging-e2e/decisions.md

# Internal CI / build artifacts
.gitlab-ci.yml
.gitlab/
# .github/workflows/ — granular: strip the internal CI workflows but keep
# the public CodeQL config (which IS meant to ship to public GitHub).
